{{!-- What goes inside one menu link: the item's icon, if the publication has that turned on, and
its label.

Ghost's `navigationIcons` lab (a public beta, so any buyer can switch it on today) lets a menu item
carry an icon with **no label at all** — the helper only drops items that have neither. A theme that
renders `{{label}}` and nothing else therefore turns such an item into an empty, nameless link. This
is the shape Ghost's own default navigation template uses, applied to all four of MIRROR's
renderings, so the bar, the panel, the footer columns and the slim row cannot disagree.

`{{@navigationIcons}}` is set by the navigation helper on the frame it renders this partial with, so
it is only ever true when the lab is on.

One line, and trimmed at both ends: the bar's current item is marked with a bottom border, and a
stray whitespace text node inside that link would widen it. Params: `iconSize` (height utility for
the artwork). --}}
{{~#if @navigationIcons~}}{{~#if icon~}}<img src="{{icon}}" alt="{{iconAlt}}" class="{{iconSize}} inline-block w-auto align-[-0.125em]">{{~/if~}}{{~label~}}{{~else~}}{{~label~}}{{~/if~}}
